**Requirement (Lifecycle measurement by owner)** · `req:nrz:decision-lifecycle-measurements`

Each implementation lane measures its own new lifecycle: cumulative Work, staged/output/retained bytes, cache hits and misses, runtime and peak memory, with exact N/N−1 and prior-usage limits where applicable. CAS owns graph/certificate replay costs, bindings owns physical checks and evidence attachments, scalar owns enclosure arithmetic, matrix owns snapshot/version/storage and numerical execution, and physics owns plan/point scheduling. Refinement charges every attempt to the original allowance. These are measurement obligations; no runtime or allocation result is inferred from this design, and no CAS cost implementation is included.

**Example (Ordinary native selection baseline costs)** · `ex:nrz:decision-native-selection-costs`

The ordinary CAS baseline measures a local box-membership assumption followed by native selection under unchanged defaults. For the cycle box, membership costs 29,300 Work and selection costs 956,428 generation plus 1,715,691 checker Work; their staged thresholds are 20,816 and 169,741 bytes. For the negative sign box the corresponding Work figures are 29,340, 742,533 and 1,336,868, with 20,848 and 168,496 staged bytes. The upper-left box admits ordinary local membership at 43,786 Work and 33,120 staged bytes, but native selection reaches a pending exact-region obligation at 208,643 generation Work and 37,817 staged bytes. The fixture uses one association to isolate these costs; neither its ordinary hypothesis nor its selected local equality proves an enclosure origin or the required complete decision partition. Exact certified admission remains an implementation obligation of the CAS owner in (`req:nrz:decision-owner-cas-judgments`).

**Rule (Implemented rational case-cut boundary)** · `rule:nrz:decision-cut-implementation`

The CAS exposes a pure rational cut query over exact native association identities and closed Real or Integer coordinate boxes (`rule:nrz:cas-decision-cut-boundary`), (`rule:nrz:decision-mixed-cut-implementation`). It checks rational affine predicates, sign and equality boundaries, and an Integer-sorted rational option literal in an explicit integer range. It publishes no witness, hypothesis or selected descriptor and does not establish an enclosure origin or complete partition. Native associations accept Integer results checked against the declared case sort; an integral Real option refuses an integer-cell question (`rule:nrz:cas-piecewise-integer-results`), (`rule:nrz:cas-piecewise-decision-boundary`). Qualified introduction is a separate checked consumer of this prerequisite (`rule:nrz:decision-certified-frame-implementation`). General input-family replay beyond the closed rational subset (`rule:nrz:decision-closed-rational-replay`), non-rational separating lemmas and general parametric cover beyond (`rule:nrz:decision-parameter-family-implementation`) remain with the CAS owner (`rule:nrz:decision-exact-certificate`), (`req:nrz:decision-owner-cas-judgments`).

**Rule (Implemented finite rational partition boundary)** · `rule:nrz:decision-partition-implementation`

A separate finite partition checker reconstructs globally total rational affine predicates, requires each nonconstant comparison to use one coordinate after cancellation, and exhausts their exact Cartesian cells (`rule:nrz:cas-decision-partition-boundary`). It accepts the sign trichotomy, a bounded integer family and all seven phase-chart regions, rejecting missing singletons or axes, overlaps even with equal values, empty domains and options outside the domain. Finite integer declarations retain both integral endpoints and match every option to its exact unit cell. The sealed caller-owned check is tied to its immutable case, ordered coordinates and optional range; retaining it avoids repeating partition reconstruction for subsequent cuts. It has no global cache, wire representation, proof record or hypothesis authority, so it cannot substitute for an elimination cover or authenticate the target enclosure (`def:nrz:decision-partition`), (`rule:nrz:decision-exact-certificate`), (`rule:nrz:decision-hypothesis-use`).

