**Rule (Implemented closed rational replay subset)** · `rule:nrz:decision-closed-rational-replay`

The CAS's `RationalEnclosure` binds an exact original target to its context, that context's admitted family, an included rational interval and an origin naming the identical target (`rule:nrz:cas-closed-enclosure-replay`). `ExactRational` requires an exact rational result; `PiBound` independently checks the finite Machin expansion and its outward interval, then propagates rational bounds through the closed target (`rule:nrz:cas-pi-machin-bounds`). Both inspect every original operand before normalization. Changed identities, false arithmetic, inward bounds, unsupported kernel origins and provenance-only claims refuse. The sealed result is a caller-owned prerequisite; separate introduction checks coordinate correspondence and retains the complete proof (`rule:nrz:decision-certified-frame-implementation`). Free-input interval arguments, other transcendental bounds and numerical attachments remain outside this subset (`req:nrz:decision-owner-certificate-origins`).

